{"id": "EUVD-2026-86133", "enisaUuid": "b93aeb3d-8384-335f-b3d3-a79c8b591e09", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nlocking/lockdep: Fix NULL pointer dereference in __lock_set_class()\n\nregister_lock_class() can return NULL when the lock class pool is\nexhausted, graph_lock() fails, or key validation fails. However,\n__lock_set_class() uses the return value directly in pointer arithmetic\nwithout a NULL check:\n\n  class = register_lock_class(lock, subclass, 0);\n  hlock->class_idx = class - lock_classes;\n\nIf class is NULL, this computes a wild offset that corrupts\nhlock->class_idx. The subsequent reacquire_held_locks() call will\ninvoke hlock_class() with this corrupted index, leading to a NULL or\nout-of-bounds pointer dereference.\n\nAdd the missing NULL check, consistent with how __lock_acquire() already\nhandles this case at the same call site.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T15:51:59", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:08:14", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f6093ff67ea6e347574819ed23e96e0f82a25ffc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/59a5c7dd331a3dab48100e1ef8e9bb4f9132a2b2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f56e54fd24f05e9de528fcb77f6084f80c8066ce", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5c3bff6cf26e6a54fbf8b893a879c32824d2d50d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b2113dcd8238bf00ce37a34e67b29cf31d32a545", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e7c69c6695d84220847cca62a45e879e71e79e9d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9be10f49dfc2e4b472b3a5f346483b67374774b8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7577e00b9ab506202b9f1a33de3cc8cc6413a4db"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93261", "GHSA-mh76-8wxp-345h"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1f9878ed-18ab-39b7-8efe-3f4017452cef", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "64aa348edc617dea17bbd01ddee4e47886d5ec8c <b2113dcd8238bf00ce37a34e67b29cf31d32a545"}, {"id": "316d1f0b-b65e-34ec-be6e-5651724c29f6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "64aa348edc617dea17bbd01ddee4e47886d5ec8c <7577e00b9ab506202b9f1a33de3cc8cc6413a4db"}, {"id": "3d3a3084-6caf-3df6-9ef4-0f3110fa420a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "49296625-0fd6-3add-8079-4189500bfb64", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "64aa348edc617dea17bbd01ddee4e47886d5ec8c <59a5c7dd331a3dab48100e1ef8e9bb4f9132a2b2"}, {"id": "5c0cc937-a760-3428-8e05-a8e2de1c5609", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "5ce595a3-2d03-3bb1-89b6-63a36438da98", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "6539bbc2-00b7-3408-ac80-d122750de92e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "69649963-4b7c-356f-aeb7-bdb501c57151", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.270"}, {"id": "713e55ca-5303-373e-a4b2-99156a411d84", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "9ae0b78d-d91d-30b6-bbdd-52505b73d52a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "a7bc9ae5-f764-3737-9d31-5d9000f09eb6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "64aa348edc617dea17bbd01ddee4e47886d5ec8c <f6093ff67ea6e347574819ed23e96e0f82a25ffc"}, {"id": "c267a6d1-ca2f-3f36-a7c3-8fae95641ba2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "64aa348edc617dea17bbd01ddee4e47886d5ec8c <f56e54fd24f05e9de528fcb77f6084f80c8066ce"}, {"id": "c28dd7cb-9b19-3a28-97c0-295a0ac22c28", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "cf451182-615a-3b11-86e6-928fa9d1ee0a", "prod